  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "«To like»: «gostar de»",
     "texto": [
      "In Portuguese, «gostar» works like English «to like»: the person is the subject, as in «eu adoro» (I love), and what is liked always takes **de**: **Gosto de café** = I like coffee (literally, «I like of coffee»).",
      "It is conjugated like any -ar verb: gosto, gostas, gosta, gostamos, gostam.",
      "**Gostas de peixe?** = do you like fish? **Não gosto de carne** = I don't like meat. **Gosto muito** = I like it a lot."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "With verbs",
     "texto": [
      "Also with **de**: **Gosto de cozinhar** (I like cooking), **gosto de comer** (I like eating).",
      "Other verbs of likes, these without «de»: **adoro** (I love), **detesto** (I hate) and **prefiro** (I prefer)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
